    "probe_text": "I now have the complete pipeline. Here's the full picture.\n\n## POST /api/owners \u2014 validations and side-effects, in order\n\n**Gate (before the pipeline runs):** the endpoint is guarded by `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`, so a caller lacking that role is rejected (`AuthorizationDeniedException`) before any step. Every step below runs inside one shared transaction (`govern: [ transaction ]`), committed once at the end.\n\n| # | Step | What it does | Kind |\n|---|------|--------------|------|\n| 1 | **RecallIdempotentOwner** | Reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header. If that key already produced an owner, throws `IdempotentReplayException` (the original owner is returned, nothing new created). Otherwise publishes the key for step 20. | validation / short-circuit + side-effect (publishes key) |\n| 2 | **ValidateOwnerFields** | Reads the request body (the only step that binds `@RequestBody`). Requires non-blank `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone`, and an address (either a non-blank `addressLine1` **or** a non-blank flat `address`). Collects **all** missing fields and throws `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (400) if any. Publishes the validated body. | validation |\n| 3 | **EnsureRegistrationDateNotFuture** | If a `registrationDate` is supplied and is after today, throws `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400). Omitted date is allowed (defaulted later). | validation |\n| 4 | **EnsureValidPostcode** | Postcode is optional; if present it must be a well-formed 4-digit code valid for the city's region, else `InvalidPostcodeException` (400). | validation |\n| 5 | **NormalizeOwnerTelephone** | Rewrites `telephone` in place to canonical E.164; throws `InvalidTelephoneException` (400) if it can't. | side-effect (mutation) + validation |\n| 6 | **NormalizeOwnerEmail** | Email optional; if present, lower-cases/trims it in place and validates syntax, else `InvalidEmailException` (400). | side-effect (mutation) + validation |\n| 7 | **EnsureEmailNotDisposable** | If email present and its domain is on the disposable blocklist, throws `DisposableEmailDomainException` (400). | validation |\n| 8 | **NormalizeOwnerAddress** | Rewrites the address in place to canonical form (trim, collapse, upper-case, expand abbreviations); recomposes the flat `address` from the structured lines. | side-effect (mutation) |\n| 9 | **EnsureCityHasCapacity** | If the owner's city already holds \u2265 50 owners (case-insensitive), throws `CityAtCapacityException` (409). | validation |\n| 10 | **EnsureDailyOwnerLimit** | If \u2265 100 owners were already registered on today's business day, throws `DailyOwnerLimitException` (429). | validation |\n| 11 | **BuildOwner** | Maps the validated DTO into a new `Owner` entity via `OwnerMapper`; publishes it. | side-effect (entity creation) |\n| 12 | **AssignHousehold** | If the owner has a postcode, stamps a deterministic `householdId` (from last name + postcode). No postcode \u2192 left unstamped. | side-effect (mutation) |\n| 13 | **EnsureUniqueIdentity** | Duplicate block: if the computed `householdId` already belongs to a non-deleted owner, throws `DuplicateIdentityException` (409) \u2014 **unless** the request sets `sharesHousehold: true`, or there's no postcode/household. | validation |\n| 14 | **FlagPossibleDuplicate** | Records `possibleDuplicateOf` = id of the earliest non-deleted owner sharing last name + postcode but a different telephone. Declared household members are never flagged (set to null). Owner is still created either way. | side-effect (mutation) |\n| 15 | **ResolveOwnerRegistrationDate** | Sets the effective `registrationDate`: the supplied date, or today if none; then rolls a weekend forward to Monday (business day). | side-effect (mutation) |\n| 16 | **AssignOwnerCustomerCode** | Assigns `customerCode` = `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from postcode, hash of E.164 telephone + last name), de-duplicated with a `-<n>` suffix if it collides with an existing code. | side-effect (mutation) |\n| 17 | **CountNamesakes** | Sets `namesakeCount` = number of existing owners sharing first+last name (case-insensitive), before this owner is persisted (so it isn't counted). | side-effect (mutation) |\n| 18 | **AssignMembershipLevel** | Computes and sets `membershipPoints` (from email presence, namesake count, household size+1, tenure in fiscal years) and the derived `membershipLevel`. | side-effect (mutation) |\n| 19 | **SaveOwner** | Persists the owner via `OwnerRepository.save` (assigns its id). | side-effect (persistence) |\n| 20 | **RecordIdempotentOwner** | Associates the `Idempotency-Key` (from step 1) with the new owner's id, so a repeat replays it. No key \u2192 records nothing. | side-effect (persistence) |\n| 21 | **AuditOwnerCreated** | Logs one line to the `AUDIT` logger (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipPoints, membershipLevel, membershipNumber). | side-effect (logging) |\n| 22 | **RespondWithOwnerCreated** | Builds `OwnerDto` and sends `201 Created` with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`. | side-effect (response) |\n\n### Notable ordering points\n- **Idempotency is checked first** (step 1), before any validation or the duplicate check, so a replay short-circuits everything.\n- **Field validation precedes** all business rules (steps 2\u20134), so a bad body is a 400 rather than being masked by a later conflict.\n- **Normalization happens before the checks that depend on it** \u2014 telephone \u2192 E.164 before the customer-code hash (16); email lower-cased/validated (6) before the disposable-domain check (7).\n- **Household id is stamped (12) before the uniqueness (13) and possible-duplicate (14) checks**, both of which key off it.\n- Steps 9, 10, 13, 14, 16, 17, 18 all read `ownerRepository.findAll()`; the new owner isn't yet persisted, so it's excluded from those counts until step 19."
